    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0267" n="259" xml:id="pg259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.5151/1701: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-31T10:00:00-05:00">January 31, 1938—10
                        a.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>52. For Cochran from Secretary of the Treasury.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d205-f1"/>
                    Your 160. The reference to the Tripartite Agreement and France which the French
                    Financial Attaché to the United States reported to Rueff was given only as
                    background information to the press and not as a direct statement or interview.
                    In the circumstances Secretary Morgenthau does not wish his name to be used in
                    connection with it.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d205-f1" n="10" xml:id="d205-f1-content">
                <p>Marginal note: “Telephoned by Mr. Lochhead, Treasury Department.”</p>
            </note>
